      <!-- Was a static stock photo (editorial-barefield.jpg), then briefly a
           live Cloudflare Radar rotator (functions/api/radar.js — left in
           place, unused, in case this comes back) — replaced with a
           decorative autoplay runner game, security-reskinned. Pure attract
           mode: never reads input, dies and restarts forever, purely
           ambient like the nebula ships / subliminal glitch layer. AI jump
           timing uses a fixed reaction distance that doesn't scale with the
           game's own speed ramp — deliberate, so it plays cleanly at first
           and eventually mistimes a jump as it speeds up, giving each run a
           natural ~15-25s length instead of running forever or looking
           obviously scripted. -->
      <figure class="ed-frame ed-frame--b ed-arcade" aria-label="Decorative animation: an autoplaying security-themed runner game, not interactive">
        <span class="ed-bento__lbl ed-arcade__lbl">Auto-defense · watching the perimeter<span class="ed-arcade__score" id="ed-arcade-score">0000</span></span>
